      "writtenOn": "2017-07-10T03:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we move this code to Nat464Xlat.java?\n\nEvery Nat464Xlat object already has access to the ConnectivityService handler and NetworkManagementService reference.\n\nPersonally I don\u0027t think this belongs in ConnectivityService, and even if it does, CS is so large that it\u0027s a good idea to move code to other files instead of keeping it all here. Existing examples are PacketKeepaliveTracker and NetworkAgentInfo, both of which contain code that runs inline on the ConnectivityService handler thread.\n\nPutting it in Nat464Xlat also has the advantage that it will be able to access instance fields such as mIface and mBaseIface, if it needs to.\n\nI think it could also simplify this code by removing some null guards.\n\nAlso, I think it would improve readability because it would encapsulate most of the 464xlat state management and lifecycle in one file.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4539,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4569,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c137a489bd7819b3c85de0a4bccffdb3236918f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
